From: SaaiOS <os@saaios>
Subject: synaptics td4150: since28 loop 0x45 until remaining==0

since27 sent chunk 0, then IDENTIFY 0x10 / mode 0x02. write_message
treated that as STATUS_OK, logged a hardcoded "0x1b complete", and
broke out of the 24-chunk loop. zeroflash claimed firmware started.
Chunks 1..23 never left the host (~4k of 97k). Same stub as the old
u16-wrap truncation.

1. Loop until remaining==0. A successful chunk is not "firmware started."
2. Log the actual status that completed the chunk (0x01 / 0x10 / 0x1b).
3. IDENTIFY 0x10 / mode 0x02 with remaining>0: log aborted early, do not
   claim firmware started, do not send more RomBoot 0x45.
4. Stock 0x45 payload header is 14 reserved bytes: [0]=size>>16 (24-bit
   TOTAL high byte), [1..13]=0, firmware at 14. No chunk index / type.
   Stock left [1][2] zero because the TCM u16 length carried the rest on
   an unchunked write. Complete the 24-bit BE total so chunk 0 is not
   read as ~4096. TCM length field stays TOTAL payload, never chunk_space.
5. Keep: first drain, no lcd_rst, no IRQ flood, no ENABLE_REPORT 0x05,
   no do_polling, no IRQ unwind, skip-0x30 / helper only after remaining==0.

Applies after syna-tcm-romboot-0x1b-chunk.patch.

